            },
            {
                "user_message": "And how payments work?",
                "assistant_message": "The payment system on Shakers works by following these steps:\n\n1. Clients create a project with a set budget or hourly rate.\n2. Once a freelancer is hired, the client funds the project by placing the agreed amount in escrow.\n3. For fixed-price projects, clients can create milestones and release payments as deliverables are completed.\n4. For hourly projects, freelancers log their hours using the time-tracking system, and clients are billed weekly.\n5. Once the client approves the work, the funds are released to the freelancer's Shakers account.\n6. Freelancers can withdraw their earnings through various methods like bank transfers, PayPal, and other payment services [Document: Payment System in Shakers].",
